language js

// `as never` — the bottom type is assignable to EVERY other type, so this
// silences any assignment error in one word. It is a strictly stronger escape
// hatch than `as any`, and biome ships no built-in rule for it.
//
// Scoped at biome.json's ROOT since 2026-08-27, so it covers src/, bin/ and
// test/ alike. It sat in the `test/**` override until `src/`'s last 2 sites
// were drained (webhook-serve-compat.ts passed `undefined as never` for the
// `this` and `server` arguments of a fetch handler; both now receive the real
// in-memory server object). An override entry would silently re-narrow it.
//
// This is the ONLY gate on the shape. It replaced the `asNever` counter in
// scripts/check-test-escape-hatches.ts, which retired on 2026-08-27: that
// counter was text, its glob missed `.tsx` for the whole drain, and its whole
// remaining residue was prose. A regex kept as a "secondary guard" behind a
// working rule guards nothing.
//
// Because nothing else watches this shape, the wiring is pinned behind
// test/unit/scripts/biome-no-as-never-plugin.test.ts.
`$expr as never` where {
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $expr,
    message = "`as never` silences every assignment error. Complete the fixture, tighten the helper's return type, or narrow the parameter — see .nax/rules/test-ratchets.md."
  )
}
